subtasks.description:
To further help identifying the various accounts sending through Mandrill -and to act as a backup as the API key, we need to add a header for the subaccount when sending an email. This is as simple as adding this before the usual "Send" logic:

```
var msg = new MailMessage();

// This adds a new header with the subaccount in (needs to be set/called/added after creating the MailMessage object)
msg.Headers.Add("X-MC-Subaccount", "domain.com");

// This is your usual sending logic (no need to change)
var smtpClient = new SmtpClient();
smtpClient.Send(msg);
```

If using the more recent versions of our contact us form you need to set the web.config key `Mandrill.Subaccount`
